  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "The current best is config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) at 0.6501. The key open question is whether adding visual information can improve upon this, but the only prior image result (resnet50, singleprofile) was very weak (0.2079), leaving it unclear whether a stronger image encoder (ViT-L) would contribute meaningfully. Config_036 tests multimodal fusion using all the best-known RNA settings (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) combined with the strongest available image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) and simple concat fusion. This is the highest-information experiment: if it beats 0.6501, we unlock a promising multimodal direction for the remaining 3 experiments; if it does not, we confirm RNA-only is the ceiling and can spend remaining budget refining RNA-only configurations (e.g., transformer aggregation with scvi_n200). Using ViT-L rather than resnet50 is critical because resnet50's poor standalone performance may simply reflect a weak encoder, and testing multimodal with a known-weak image encoder would not resolve the core question."
}

